{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And they shall hang.</b> After he compared him to a peg, he said, 'and they shall hang upon it.'" "<b>The offspring.</b> They are the sons, for they are those who go forth from the bowels." "<b>And the vessels.</b> Perhaps they are the daughters, from the root of יצא צפע (Isaiah 14:29). And after he said that he is a father, behold: the men of Judah are like his sons, and the women like his daughters, for they are likened to small vessels." "And the meaning of <b>of the vessels of the bowls</b> is like 'and he placed in basins' (Exodus 24:6); perhaps it is a name for the gold." "<b>And all the vessels of the stringed instruments.</b> Instruments of music. And the meaning is that nothing will remain in the royal house that is not under his authority."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:45.186449059Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}